In a file with only comments, the header comment ends at the first blank line, so only its first `//` line prints.
== args
input/comment-only-blank-break.rs
== file input/comment-only-blank-break.rs
// First line is part of header.

// This line is not contiguous and must be excluded.
== stdout
input/comment-only-blank-break.rs (3 lines)
First line is part of header.
